   "text": "I read the structure in three parts and then worked out each stereocentre from the wedges and hashes.\n\n**Structure**\n- **Aryl ester:** a 2,4,6-trichlorobenzoate ester, with Cl on the two ortho positions and the para position.\n- **Pyridine:** the ring nitrogen is next to the carbon bearing the amide C(=O)NH. The next carbon carries the trichlorobenzoyloxy group, and the one after that carries OMe.\n- **Nine-membered dilactone ring**, going round from the NH-bearing carbon:\n  - CH(NH-amide)\n  - C(=O)\n  - O\n  - CH(CH3)\n  - CH(O-isobutyrate)\n  - CH(CH2Ph)\n  - C(=O)\n  - O\n  - CH2, which closes back to the NH-bearing carbon\n- **Substituents:** the isobutyrate is OC(=O)CH(CH3)2 and the benzyl group is CH2Ph.\n\n**Stereochemistry (four centres)**\n- The NH-bearing carbon has the N on a hashed bond.\n- The CH(CH3) carbon has the methyl on a wedge.\n- The CH(O-isobutyrate) carbon has the ester oxygen on a hashed bond.\n- The CH(CH2Ph) carbon has the benzyl group on a wedge.\n\nI assigned @/@@ for each centre by taking the neighbour order in the SMILES and comparing it with the drawn geometry, with the implicit H on the side opposite the wedged or hashed substituent.\n\nSMILES: COc1ccnc(C(=O)N[C@H]2COC(=O)[C@H](Cc3ccccc3)[C@@H](OC(=O)C(C)C)[C@@H](C)OC2=O)c1OC(=O)c1c(Cl)cc(Cl)cc1Cl"
